briefs:
{company} in {city} changed every password this week, and the new ones are long. Breaking the admin password would take most people far too long.

So do not break it. Their public notices are open to anyone who logs in as a guest. Read them. Work out who resets passwords there and who they would do it for, then write to them from the Phishing window as that person. When the reply comes you will have the admin login.

Then do the job: {goal}

The job at {company} is simple: {goal}

The hard part is the admin password, which they have just made much stronger. A letter is quicker than a cracker. Log in as a guest, read the staff notices, and write to their IT person as the one colleague they would not refuse. Mention what that colleague would know.

If you would rather break the password the long way, that is up to you.

